- (5) Permit for Conditional Use of Soil Amendments: The purpose of this permit is to ensure compliance with the one-hundred (100) foot soil amendment buffer in subsection (4), to safeguard residents of Warren County from nuisance, to prevent unauthorized disposal of industrial waste and by-products, and to confirm that any soil amendment has complied with applicable state law before it is manufactured, stored, or applied. Granting of the permit shall be conditioned on the following:

- (i) Enforcement Survey. Upon request for a “Permit for Conditional Use of Soil Amendments’ and before the issuance of any such permit, the Administrator shall survey the property on which the soil amendment is to be applied and confirm with the party seeking the permit that the boundaries of such application shall be at least one-hundred (100) feet from the areas subject to conditional use as defined in subsection (4) above. The Administrator may measure this distance and may identify, mark, or record the physical boundaries for the authorized application of any soil amendment.

In considering whether to grant a permit, the Administrator shall consider the presence and location of any beneficial plants, animals, or aquatic life either within the confines of or adjacent to the application site for the purposes of preserving their respective habitats and benefits. This determination may

