include factors such as, but not limited to, elevation, run-off, soil composition, air quality, and risk of contamination.

The Administrator shall issue and retain a copy of the survey of the property and showing any findings made in accordance with this subsection.

- (ii) Agreement for Permit for Conditional Use of Soil Amendments. As part of the permit application process, the party seeking the permit shall complete the “Agreement for Permit for Conditional Use of Soil Amendments.” This written agreement shall be notarized and filed with the Administrator and include the following:

- 1. The name(s) and signature(s) of the parties seeking the permit; 2. The date of the agreement;

- 3. The plats and addresses of the property where the soil amendment shall be applied, including depictions of all adjacent property and water sources;

4, The specifications of the application boundaries, including the forms of demarcation; distance from any adjacent restricted district, property, or water sources, along with any accompanying exhibits;

- 5. An agreement that the application of the soil amendment(s) shall not come within one-hundred (100) feet of any restricted district, water source, or property without consent of the property owner per Sec. 5.9.5(b)(6);

- 6. An agreement that the Administrator may further restrict the area of application to prevent harm to beneficial plants, animals, and aquatic life;

- 7. An agreement that any transportation of the soil amendment(s) from an industrial district and on-site storage at the property where the amendment(s) shall be applied shall not exceed twelve (12) hours combined;

- 8. The bona fide agricultural purpose for the soil amendment(s). This statement shall include the specific item(s) from the definition of “agricultural operation” in Sec. 2.1 and the contemplated schedule for said operation along with its total estimated duration;

- 9. Whether the applicant is an “agricultural facility” as defined in Sec. 2.1 or otherwise engaged in commercial agriculture;

- 10. An agreement any excess or unused soil amendments shall not be stored on-site more than twelve (12) hours and not be disposed of on-site under any conditions;

