- (iii) This permit shall have effect for the duration of the agricultural operation specified in the written agreement, which period shall not exceed onehundred and eighty (180) days. Renewal of the permit shall require a new survey by the Administrator and signing a new agreement.

- (iv) Permit approval is subject to the Administrator's review of the certificate of code enforcement survey and the written agreement.

- (v) The application fee for said permit shall be five-hundred dollars ($500.00) plus fifteen dotlars ($15.00) per acre on which the party seeks to use soil amendments. This fee shall be payable to the Administrator.

- (vi) If any state or federal court issues any judgment or ruling that the use of any soil amendment on property within the boundaries of Warren County constitutes a nuisance as defined in Sec. 2.2 or otherwise within the meaning of the law, any permit issued by Warren County to use that soil amendment on the subject property shall stand revoked.
